\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Jesus, the bruises that you had,
\par \pard\li225\sl186\slmult0 the torchuring death that you died
\par gives me contentment and blessing
\par in my suffering moments
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par should evil fill up my mind
\par your suffering is before me
\par this does not give me the chance to
\par associate myself with sin again.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Should the flesh, it's many pleasures
\par \pard\li225\sl186\slmult0 are about to worry me
\par when I remember your suff'ring
\par it drives away the serpent
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par if satan also draws near
\par and is about to tempt me
\par I only point to him your cross
\par he goes away and am relieved
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. And in all my tribulations
\par \pard\li315\sl186\slmult0 I at once remember yours
\par If I deeply think of it too
\par I am encouraged by that
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par your many comforting words
\par have made me to have my peace
\par because  you died for me also
\par for my soul also to be saved.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl186\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. You, to whom I much look up to
\par \pard\li315\sl186\slmult0  You who are my hiding place
\par and your death has overcome death
\par and it can no more harm me
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par because you are on my side
\par and so I am not afraid
\par He is my light in my darkness
\par I will receive life, eternal.
\par \pard\li144\sl80\slmult0 
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

